that is subject to Title I of ERISA; a plan, as defined in section 4975(e)(1) of the Code, that is subject to Section 4975 of the Code, including individual retirement accounts and Keogh plans; and an entity whose underlying assets include plan
assets by reason of a plan&#146;s investment in that entity, including insurance company general accounts. A Plan fiduciary considering an investment in the Units </FONT></P> <P STYLE="margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"><FONT
SIZE="1">&nbsp;</FONT></P>
 <P STYLE="margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px" ALIGN="center"><FONT FACE="Times New Roman" SIZE="2">55 </FONT></P>


