 <P STYLE="margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px; text-indent:4%"><FONT FACE="Times New Roman" SIZE="2"><I>Exception for Publicly Offered Securities.</I> The plan asset regulations provide that the issuer of a
publicly-offered security acquired by a Plan will not be deemed to hold Plan assets solely because of that acquisition. A publicly-offered security is a security that is &#147;freely transferable,&#148; part of a class of securities that is owned by
100 or more investors independent of the issuer and of one another and either: </FONT></P> <P STYLE="margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:-6px"><FONT SIZE="1">&nbsp;</FONT></P>
